# Server Management Rule

**CRITICAL: The agent must NEVER start or kill services/servers, whether frontend or backend servers, unless specifically instructed by the user.**

## Prohibited Actions
- **DO NOT start new servers** (frontend or backend)
- **DO NOT kill existing servers** (frontend or backend)
- **DO NOT restart services** (frontend or backend)
- **DO NOT manage server processes** in any way

## Why This Rule Exists
When making code changes:
- Simply save the files - changes will be applied automatically
- The development servers will hot-reload the changes
- No manual server management is required

## What This Applies To
This prohibition applies to ALL types of servers and services:
- Frontend development server (typically running on port 3000 or similar)
- Backend development server (typically running on port 8000 or similar)
- Any other development or production servers
- Database services
- Any background processes or services

## Important Note
The development environment is configured for hot-reloading, so code changes are automatically applied without any server intervention needed.